1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,563
Trained from scratch.

2
00:00:01,563 --> 00:00:02,609
In India.

3
00:00:02,609 --> 00:00:05,000
On those shared chips you just saw.

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,010
And before it ever talked to you, it read around twelve trillion pieces of text.

5
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:12,547
Then Sarvam did something generous.

6
00:00:12,547 --> 00:00:14,455
It made the model open.

7
00:00:14,455 --> 00:00:19,293
Any Indian developer can download it and build their own apps on it, for free.

8
00:00:19,293 --> 00:00:23,821
The minister had hoped for six months, and later said ten at the most.

9
00:00:23,821 --> 00:00:25,352
It took about a year.

10
00:00:25,352 --> 00:00:28,530
Late, you could say... but delivered.

11
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:32,478
And that same week, BharatGen — a team led by I.I.T.

12
00:00:32,478 --> 00:00:38,529
Bombay — showed its own model too, called Param Two, built for all twenty-two scheduled Indian languages.

13
00:00:38,529 --> 00:00:40,262
Now remember my promise to you.

14
00:00:40,262 --> 00:00:41,561
The chopping test.

15
00:00:41,561 --> 00:00:42,654
Same question.

16
00:00:42,654 --> 00:00:44,607
Will it rain in my village tomorrow?

17
00:00:44,607 --> 00:00:46,727
DeepSeek's chopper, you've seen.

18
00:00:46,727 --> 00:00:48,063
Hindi, eighteen.

19
00:00:48,063 --> 00:00:49,574
Marathi, twenty.

20
00:00:49,574 --> 00:00:51,118
Telugu, twenty-five.

21
00:00:51,118 --> 00:00:53,972
The chopper behind Chat G.P.T.'s recent models...

22
00:00:53,972 --> 00:00:57,585
Hindi eight, Marathi fourteen, Telugu fifteen.

23
00:00:57,585 --> 00:00:58,684
And Sarvam's?

24
00:00:58,684 --> 00:01:01,636
Hindi, eight — exactly the same as English.

25
00:01:01,636 --> 00:01:02,986
Marathi, ten.

26
00:01:02,986 --> 00:01:04,370
Telugu, eleven.

27
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:06,489
And this isn't one lucky sentence.

28
00:01:06,489 --> 00:01:11,992
We ran the same test on more than a thousand sentences, each one in thirteen languages.

29
00:01:11,992 --> 00:01:13,146
Look at Odia.

30
00:01:13,146 --> 00:01:17,010
On DeepSeek's chopper, five and a half times the pieces of English.

31
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:19,564
On Sarvam's... less than one and a half.

32
00:01:19,564 --> 00:01:22,281
And BharatGen's chopper does about as well.

33
00:01:22,281 --> 00:01:25,705
So for your language, the gap shrinks, a lot.

34
00:01:25,705 --> 00:01:29,360
Because this time... an Indian team put the missing pieces in.

